{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":39,"timestamp":"2026-09-19T01:36:01.281674Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"745c7d7d-45f4-4cd0-a98d-474a1eac682f","comment_uuid":"1e2ea5b3-aca5-4284-b65a-ace1a493ca39","author":"xqjG","content":"PASS 2 (Tier A) COMPLETE: Ch17 Ontologies (Frank Chen), Ch10 Agents for O11y (Boris Tane), Ch21 LLM O11y (Phillip Carter), Ch7 agents-instrument section, Ch8 GenAI-analysis section — 49 pages via PDFKit text extraction (offset PDF=book+36), ~115KB/~30k tokens read inline, zero fan-out. Pass-1 cost ~9k. LOAD-BEARING MAPPINGS FOR VSDD: (1) Ch17's ontology for nondeterministic systems IS vsdd's architecture: nouns+invariants+ActionPlan('parsed intent, untrusted until validated')+3 CI gates (deterministic/simulation/semantic)+universal payload+signal parity ('the assertion that blocks the PR is the same query that fires the incident'). The MISSING NOUN in vsdd: a dispatch-plan object with predicted cost/width that the run record is validated against (simulation gate = chosen-vs-observed mechanized; the 2.56x overrun becomes proposal_status=rejected, rejection_reason=simulation_mismatch on a record, not a comment). (2) Predictability for nondeterministic systems = constrain the OUTPUT with invariants + trace the run, NOT predict the input (my advisory band was input-side; hard budget + width caps are invariants). (3) Slice 6 record shape = Ch17 universal payload + Ch21 GenAI semconv: identity/versions (contract hash, primer, template, model, effort), invariant results (SHOULD hash, WAS-superset verdict, cap hit), cost (tokens in/out/cache per agent, steps), outcome classes, large I/O by LINK not inline, operator feedback signal (kill/override) as attribute. (4) GH#33 answers from Ch21: store (model, tokens) per row and DERIVE cost at query time (never store dollars) so prompt/model versions compare cleanly; latency is a dimension on the same wide event, not a second ledger; staleness trigger = any change to model/prompt/harness re-runs the eval set; task evals score STEPS TAKEN + tokens + specific conclusions — the three axes of a dispatch efficiency record; evals have pass/fail/MAYBE (= our plausible class). (5) Reliability SLI for the harness = proposal-rejection rate (Ch17: 'highest-fidelity signal for AI reliability') — for vsdd: rate of dispatch plans rejected by verifier or killed/overridden by operator. (6) Ch10 validates R1 injection-by-construction from the o11y side and names the erosion: 'the mental model that's disappearing' — context must be a maintained first-class layer (topology, naming, known issues=deviation registry, recent incidents); operator role = direction + boundary judgment. (7) Ch8 personas: attended round = commander (Claude Code named), container kickoff = caretaker ('requires significant knowledge transfer'; error compounds with autonomy). (8) Ch7: 'automate the automation' (agent writes a script vs N per-item edits = the 28-verifier lesson in the book's words); 'treat agent rules like software' — daily CI job runs the agent, emits telemetry, independently evaluates; agent skills = shared versioned tooling. (9) Ratification worry, in the book's words: 'an ontology remains an academic exercise until it is codified' — codified = schemas+gates (harness-grade), ratified prose = convention-grade. LIMITS: Ch17 is a single contributed chapter (energy domain) — a pattern not a standard; the book has nothing on multi-agent fan-out shaping per se; eval guidance is product-facing. TIER B RECOMMENDATION: Ch18 CI/CD-as-traces + Ch22 Fin (north-star metric derivation, token-cost governance) + Ch27 activities-vs-learning (~34pp, ~25k).","created_at":"2026-09-19T01:36:01.265151Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAyMb9irl9vHDYOoEwdbMEzV8/L56Tx4sic53xTzrSdNF5j4/koYtZvb7z3imBpbcBJgW1OdQFKdKeILI5p0CdCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGXmvJucZWOIUd7RIuIv1UCnEwDcn/xcorRZNwa/BPmQZ7uc2kfoHnOJfaTG/qxVx6ihUAsB83bMuk8dxYXJ4Ao="}
{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":40,"timestamp":"2026-09-19T01:44:52.289311Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"745c7d7d-45f4-4cd0-a98d-474a1eac682f","comment_uuid":"ceec35ae-299c-4886-b541-c7e5958f13eb","author":"xqjG","content":"TIER B READ (Ch18 CI/CD, Ch22 Fin, Ch27 investment — 34pp, ~22k tokens inline) + KNOWLEDGE CAPTURED. Four pages (tags design-input/reference/observability, source = O'Reilly ISBN 9781098179922): observability-engineering-2e-reading-map (what/why/method/cost actuals, not-read list with candidates), o11y-ontology-invariants-and-the-dispatch-plan (Ch17+18: ActionPlan = the missing dispatch-plan noun; simulation gate = chosen-vs-observed mechanized; signal parity = Slice 6 spec; rejection-rate SLI; determinism hash; critical-path lesson for orchestration), o11y-llm-telemetry-evals-and-agent-context (Ch21/10/8/7: GenAI semconv, cost derived at query time, evals pass/fail/MAYBE, task evals score steps+tokens+conclusions, flywheel, context layer, personas, automate-the-automation; GH#33 four answers; Slice 6 field list), o11y-cost-attribution-feedback-loops-and-drift (Ch22/27/18: cost-per-dispatch as attribute+SLO, silent-waste class = dispatch paths emitting no vsdd record, Rasmussen 3 boundaries incl. OPERATOR WORKLOAD, activities-vs-learning as the ratification diagnostic, per-dispatch hard budgets = per-team self-governance, P90/P50 flake tax, 6-7 min attention threshold). TIER B NEW YIELD beyond Tier A: (a) the what-vs-why lesson — a top-line token total without per-agent/per-stage spans is Fin's failed first attempt; (b) silent waste hides exactly where no metric is emitted — our Workflow runs emit harness totals but no vsdd event; (c) Ch27's diagnostic question 'for each practice, can you point to the feedback mechanism that turns it into learning?' is the operator's ratification worry made operational; (d) Ch18: fan-out raises countable failures, retries hide them in the tail, and CI is the best-ROI starter surface — routing-gate/verify workflows as traces. STATUS: capture complete; IMPACT ANALYSIS (Slices 6/7, GH#33 answer, deviation registry, process artifacts) is the operator's next step, not started. Total read cost this issue: ~65k tokens, zero agents.","created_at":"2026-09-19T01:44:52.275556Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAGxao3plgy4zzij/x+6szJPFOSTf9xxfAElrNvnko/T/K4FuH50Nvf3QRcaOBM0NGez4o8SHS+z85mSvzLjUADQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFLY2tQJrhBUhFsgtaFLKkHGS7/xaSY3L3Mv63WSStwL/KZy5877nsl9K4fcloBJa0tt7enhQoQsvl6bBT7R9gE="}
