{"agent_id":"xqjG","agent_seq":45,"timestamp":"2026-09-19T02:03:53.826313Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1f8688e3-ec32-48d0-87c6-cfc9326ccd06","comment_uuid":"bd179c86-7efe-4518-afa0-8ab3c2d06186","author":"xqjG","content":"SO RULING (operator, 2026-09-18) — B5: OPTION B, regenerable dispatch rows. The Slice 7 efficiency insight engine's unit of output is one wide record per dispatch in NATIVE UNITS ONLY (identity, versions, plan, dials, per-agent usage by cache class, conformance verdict, per-field provenance tag incl. could-not-check), materialized as engine-written, mdatron-governed, repo-tracked versioned data. NOT the retired ledger: it is a CACHE of the reader's output — deletable and rebuilt byte-identically from the records. FOUR FALSIFIERS bind it: (1) a row not reproducible from its linked records fails a determinism check; (2) a row written by anything other than the engine (hand-authored) is rejected by construction; (3) a row whose source record is unavailable carries could-not-check on those fields, never a number; (4) a dollar figure in a row is a violation. HONEST LIMIT (recorded): rows do not launder the oracle — until the REQ-10 synced/corroborated transcript channel lands, every figure is could-not-check-grade in a row exactly as it would be recomputed; the row makes the tag durable and visible. ROUTE: amendment at Slice 7's phase-1a opening via the owned process (owning domain composition + cold review; SO ratifies) — targets: contract §Cost is knowable / REQ-11 ('a reader over the records, not a persisted ledger') and build-plan Phase 6 sentence ('The unit-and-dollar ledger ... retired, not built') gain the clause 'a derived, regenerable, engine-written, provenance-tagged record in native units is not the retired ledger' + the four falsifiers. Storage home (per-dispatch file vs append-only; repo vs hub) is a 1a detail under one constraint: the gate needs it repo-tracked. Rejected alternatives: pure reader (history evaporates with ~/.claude transcripts; no CI-checkable plan-vs-actual leg; nothing for viewers to hang off); tracker-comment rows (not schema-governed; N x issue-show joins, upstream #52).","created_at":"2026-09-19T02:03:53.814266Z","kind":"decision","signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAzmWqwfUbxMHZc4mH/9d8hAkwPvKthXkrNqi3kezOC7O2nLjOjSe8X2WkqGnh3FTLYoicIbJsD33NS7XNh694Ag=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:v2ahqtq1cloiYtPHwSJByIfLW+KKRz5ElCE0sStkAow","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgQ6tbyGxjDfsNHdeOlMQZQaTJX9Ij1ckKVPX/DhibsJAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD2kzzU9hikoZxgAjChwVo+jpnVi5Y52HtY3wmAeuPwbOzYaP0XHGs/wg2dBlDqKvTJyxe8mbd6lnC2PiOPQbw0="}
